{
 "problem": "Bisognano-Wichmann (A9) for Tanimoto's Borchers triple of the Bullough-Dodd S-matrix",
 "nodes": {
  "S": {
   "text": "Tanimoto's (M_T, U, Omega) is a Borchers triple for S_{1/2}: M_T is generated by the fields chi(xi), chi'(eta), Omega is cyclic and separating, U(x) M_T U(x)* is in M_T for x in the right wedge, and Haag-Ruelle scattering theory is available",
   "side": "start",
   "depth": 0
  },
  "G": {
   "text": "Bisognano-Wichmann holds on all of H: Delta_{M_T}^{it} = U(0, -2 pi t) and J_{M_T} = J, hence wedge duality M_T' = J M_T J",
   "side": "goal",
   "depth": 0
  },
  "F1": {
   "text": "Compute the modular data of (M_T, Omega) on the vacuum, one- and two-particle spaces: Delta^{it} = U(0, -2 pi t) and J_{M_T} = J on H_0 + H_1 + H_2",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "S",
   "depth": 1
  },
  "F2": {
   "text": "Build n-particle vectors as products of the fields chi(xi), chi'(eta) applied to Omega and prove the Tomita relation inductively in the particle number k",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "S",
   "depth": 1
  },
  "F3": {
   "text": "Apply the Buchholz-Lechner / Alazzawi-Lechner Bisognano-Wichmann theorem for wedge-local fields",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "S",
   "depth": 1,
   "requires": [
    "R1",
    "R2"
   ]
  },
  "F4": {
   "text": "Apply Mund's theorem that Bisognano-Wichmann follows from the particle structure of a local net",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "S",
   "depth": 1
  },
  "F5": {
   "text": "Prove the Haag-Ruelle out-states at level n are sqrt(n!) P_n(slowest x ... x fastest) for all n, identifying the scattering states",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "S",
   "depth": 1
  },
  "F6": {
   "text": "Verify the formal Tomita identity S_M = S_0 numerically at particle degrees 4 and 5",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "S",
   "depth": 1
  },
  "B1": {
   "text": "V(t) = U(0, -2 pi t) Delta_{M_T}^{-it} and I = J_{M_T} J act as the identity on every vector of H",
   "side": "bwd",
   "parent": "G",
   "depth": 1
  },
  "B2": {
   "text": "The standard subspace of M_T is contained in the free standard subspace H_0, equivalently {S_M = S_0} is dense",
   "side": "bwd",
   "parent": "G",
   "depth": 1
  },
  "B3": {
   "text": "Bisognano-Wichmann holds on the closed span of all scattering states and that span is all of H",
   "side": "bwd",
   "parent": "G",
   "depth": 1
  },
  "B4": {
   "text": "Modular nuclearity of the map M_T(x) -> Delta^{1/4} M Omega holds for all wedge translations x",
   "side": "bwd",
   "parent": "G",
   "depth": 1
  },
  "F7": {
   "text": "So U(0, -2 pi t) Delta_{M_T}^{-it} and J_{M_T} J both act as the identity on the one-particle space H_1",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "F1",
   "depth": 2
  },
  "F8": {
   "text": "Created two-particle ZF vectors are never in the domain of chi'_2 because of the kinematic pole of S at i pi/3, so no product of three fields has Omega in its domain",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "F2",
   "depth": 2
  },
  "F9": {
   "text": "Check the hypotheses: those theorems need energy or particle-number bounds on the fields",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "F3",
   "depth": 2
  },
  "F10": {
   "text": "Check the hypotheses: Mund's theorem needs a local net on double cones",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "F4",
   "depth": 2
  },
  "F11": {
   "text": "The Moller operators are unitary onto H, so the wedge-local net is asymptotically complete",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "F5",
   "depth": 2
  },
  "F12": {
   "text": "The numerical agreement holds to round-off at degrees 4 and 5",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "F6",
   "depth": 2
  },
  "B5": {
   "text": "Any unitary W that fixes Omega, commutes with translations, maps M_T into itself and is the identity on H_1 fixes every Haag-Ruelle in and out state",
   "side": "bwd",
   "parent": "B1",
   "depth": 2
  },
  "B6": {
   "text": "By Borchers' theorem Delta_{M_T}^{it} and J_{M_T} have the right commutation relations with translations, so V(t) and I commute with translations and preserve M_T",
   "side": "bwd",
   "parent": "B3",
   "depth": 2
  },
  "B7": {
   "text": "Show every vector of the form A Omega with A in M_T lies in the free domain Dom Delta_0^{1/2}",
   "side": "bwd",
   "parent": "B2",
   "depth": 2
  },
  "B8": {
   "text": "Establish the split property for wedge inclusions M_T(x) in M_T at large distances",
   "side": "bwd",
   "parent": "B4",
   "depth": 2
  },
  "F13": {
   "text": "Asymptotic completeness holds, and computing the modular data on H_1 gives U(0, -2 pi t) Delta_{M_T}^{-it} = J_{M_T} J = 1 on the one-particle space",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "F11",
   "depth": 3
  },
  "F14": {
   "text": "Asymptotic completeness holds, V(t) and I are 1 on H_1, and by Borchers theorem V(t) and I fix Omega, commute with translations and map M_T into itself",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "F13",
   "depth": 4
  },
  "F15": {
   "text": "The fixed-point lemma makes V(t) and I fix every Haag-Ruelle scattering state; by asymptotic completeness these span H, so V(t) = I = 1 on all of H",
   "side": "fwd",
   "parent": "F14",
   "depth": 5
  },
  "R1": {
   "text": "Energy bounds or particle-number bounds on the wedge-local fields hold here (hypothesis of Buchholz-Lechner / Alazzawi-Lechner Bisognano-Wichmann)",
   "side": "req",
   "for": "F3",
   "cos": 0.771
  },
  "R2": {
   "text": "A core of field polynomials applied to the vacuum hold here (hypothesis of Buchholz-Lechner / Alazzawi-Lechner Bisognano-Wichmann)",
   "side": "req",
   "for": "F3",
   "cos": 0.738
  }
 },
